spesn firmware tables (0177): SpesModem fw_files/fw_ext/fw_all from the test phone's modem partition.

The built-in tables (0099/0115) describe the iosv2 author's NON-HLOS (HyperOS 2.0.208). The spesn
phone's modem_b (= modem_a, MD5 identical; MPSS.HA.1.1.c1-00027-KD_ALL_PACK-3.21298.20,
ADSP.VT.5.4.3-00074-DIVAR-1) has the same FAT16 layout and file sizes for the modem segments, but 20 of
28 modem segment CRCs, 273 of 610 extents and 20 file sizes differ, so the CRC check would refuse it.
Regenerated read-only on the host: tools/map-modem-fat16.py modem_b.img + tools/gen-spes-modem-tables.py.
Boot with modem_part=modem_b (active slot b). On a phone with the author's firmware this table no
longer matches (CRC check refuses, nothing is loaded). Tables contain file names, sizes, offsets and
CRC32s only (checked: no serial/MAC/IMEI).

